-500 cassette deck, a desktop computer with a modern SoundBlaster sound card, and the audio recording program GoldWave.  Each cassette was recorded to a single WAV-format file at 44100 kHz, 16-bit quality, to match the quality of CD-audio. Each resulting WAV file was split at the division between Side A and Side B of the cassette, in order to make it possible for each WAV file to fit on a single 80-minute CD.</p>","language":"eng","mediatype":"audio","title":"Niven Jazz Collection: Duke Ellington Tape 73 (1958-1959)","collection":"davidwnivenjazz","publicdate":"2013-05-29 17:57:37","uploader":"jscott@archive.org","addeddate":"2013-05-29 17:57:37","boxid":"OL100020605","backup_location":"ia905701_16"},"server":"ia903203.us.archive.org","uniq":1624779155,"workable_servers":["ia903203.us.archive.org","ia803203.us.archive.org"]}